+# Base USDC Yield Vault
+
+An ERC-4626 vault on Base. Users deposit **USDC**; the strategy pairs it with **WETH** in an
+Aerodrome LP position, stakes the LP in that pool's gauge, and a keeper calls **`harvest()`** to
+claim the AERO emissions, sell them, and compound the proceeds back into the position.
+
+```
+ depositor ──USDC──> UsdcYieldVault (ERC-4626, shares "byvUSDC")
+                          │  idle USDC waits here until the keeper moves it
+                          ▼
+              AerodromeUsdcWethStrategy
+                 │  zap:  ~50% USDC ──swap──> WETH        (Slipstream CL pool, tick spacing 100)
+                 │  add:  USDC + WETH ──────> LP          (Aerodrome v2 volatile USDC/WETH pool)
+                 │  stake: LP ──────────────> gauge       (earns AERO)
+                 └─ harvest: AERO ──sell──> USDC ──fee──> treasury, rest compounds
+                    valuation: Chainlink ETH/USD, USDC/USD, AERO/USD
+```
+
+| Contract | Purpose |
+| --- | --- |
+| `src/UsdcYieldVault.sol` | ERC-4626 accounting, deposit cap, pause, exit fee, strategy migration |
+| `src/AerodromeUsdcWethStrategy.sol` | Zap, stake, harvest, unwind, oracle pricing and all swap guards |
+| `script/Deploy.s.sol` | One-shot deployment + ownership handover |
+| `script/Keeper.s.sol` | `Harvest` and `DeployIdle` — the entire keeper surface |
+
+## Build and test
+
+```bash
+forge build
+forge test                       # 50 tests
+forge test --match-path 'test/*fork*' -vv   # the fork suite, with the measured numbers logged
+```
+
+Fork tests run against Base mainnet pinned at block **50,237,000**. They use
+`https://mainnet.base.org` by default; set `BASE_RPC_URL` to use your own node. If no RPC is
+reachable, the fork tests skip themselves and the offline suite still runs (21 tests).
+
+## Deployment
+
+```bash
+export BASE_RPC_URL=...          # a Base mainnet RPC
+export OWNER=0x...               # multisig: risk params, migrations, emergency exit
+export KEEPER=0x...              # hot EOA/bot: harvest, deployIdle, pause
+export TREASURY=0x...            # receives the performance fee
+export DEPOSIT_CAP=1000000000000 # optional, USDC 6dp (1,000,000 USDC here)
+
+forge script script/Deploy.s.sol:Deploy --rpc-url $BASE_RPC_URL \
+  --account deployer --broadcast --verify
+```
+
+The script deploys the vault, deploys the strategy pointed at it, wires them together, sets the cap
+and then `transferOwnership` to `OWNER` on both. Ownership is `Ownable2Step`, so **`OWNER` must call
+`acceptOwnership()` on both contracts** to finish the handover.
+
+The strategy constructor is the deployment's safety check: it resolves the pool from the Aerodrome
+factory, the gauge from the Voter, and the CL pool from the Slipstream factory, and reverts unless
+the gauge is registered for that pool, stakes that LP, pays AERO, **and is still alive** (a killed
+gauge keeps accepting deposits but pays nothing). It also rejects price feeds that are not 8-decimal
+Chainlink aggregators. Nothing is hardcoded that the chain cannot confirm.
+
+Recommended first steps after deploy: set a low `DEPOSIT_CAP`, deposit a small amount yourself, run
+one `harvest()` cycle, and raise the cap once the numbers look right.
+
+## Keeper operation
+
+One scheduled call does everything:
+
+```bash
+STRATEGY=0x... forge script script/Keeper.s.sol:Harvest \
+  --rpc-url $BASE_RPC_URL --account keeper --broadcast
+```
+
+`harvest(minUsdcOut)`:
+
+1. `gauge.getReward()` — claims accrued AERO.
+2. Sells the AERO for USDC, with `minOut = max(minUsdcOut, oracle price − slippage)`. The onchain
+   floor is derived from Chainlink AERO/USD and USDC/USD, so a compromised keeper cannot pass `0`
+   and sandwich the sale. Pass a tighter `MIN_USDC_OUT` if you compute one off-chain.
+3. Sends `performanceFeeBps` (default 10%) of the proceeds to the treasury.
+4. Pulls whatever USDC users deposited since the last run out of the vault.
+5. Zaps the combined balance back into the staked LP position, then checks end to end that the
+   round trip did not lose more than `maxValueLossBps` (default 0.50%).
+
+Cadence: **once or twice a day** is the right starting point. Emissions accrue linearly, so
+harvesting more often only adds gas and swap fees; the tests measure a full compounding cycle at
+roughly 6.2% gross APR (below), which is not worth chasing hourly. `DeployIdle` exists for the case
+where a large deposit lands right after a harvest and you do not want it sitting idle.
+
+What the keeper cannot do: move funds anywhere except into the position, change any parameter, or
+withdraw. Its worst case is refusing to work — which costs yield, not principal. It can also
+`pause()` (owner-only to unpause), which is the right reaction to anything surprising.
+
+Monitor: `strategy.pendingRewards()`, `vault.totalAssets()`, `vault.idleAssets()`, the gauge's
+`periodFinish`/`rewardRate` (emissions can be voted away between epochs), and any `ValueLoss`,
+`PoolPriceOffOracle` or `StalePrice` revert — those mean the strategy refused a bad trade, and they
+are worth alerting on rather than retrying blindly.
+
+## Why these integrations
+
+All figures were read from Base mainnet (chain 8453) on **2026-08-20**, around block **50,237,000**,
+and the measurements are reproduced by `test/Economics.fork.t.sol`.
+
+### Yield venue — Aerodrome v2 volatile USDC/WETH pool + gauge
+
+* Pool `0xcDAC0d6c6C59727a65F871236188350531885C43` (volatile, `stable = false`), holding
+  1,795.6 WETH + 4,162,729 USDC ≈ **$8.3M**.
+* Gauge `0x519BBD1Dd8C6A94C46080E24f316c14Ee758C025`, confirmed via Voter
+  `0x16613524e02ad97eDfeF371bC883F2F5d6C480A5`: `isGauge` and `isAlive` both true, `rewardRate`
+  0.0339 AERO/s (≈ 2,931 AERO/day), `periodFinish` in the future, and **98.7%** of the LP supply is
+  staked in it.
+* Measured gross emissions **≈ 6.2% APR** for the position (`test_GaugeEmissionsApr`).
+* The LP is a plain ERC-20 and the position is full range: no NFT, no ticks, nothing to rebalance,
+  and it can never fall out of range while the keeper is asleep. That is the main reason a v1 uses
+  the v2 pool rather than a concentrated-liquidity position.
+
+The tradeoff, stated plainly: **staking in the gauge forfeits the pool's trading fees to voters.**
+The gauge forwards them to `feesVotingReward` `0x14df87824a11DC27afF185D3149E05aaa4735f60` (the pool
+currently shows 0.49 WETH + 1,294 USDC accrued to the gauge and headed there). Measuring the pool's
+fee accumulators (`index0`/`index1`) over the windows ending at the pinned block:
+
+| window | trading fees | fee APR | emissions APR |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| 30 days | $24,257 | 3.55% | 6.20% |
+| 7 days | $8,623 | 5.41% | 6.20% |
+| 1 day | $2,683 | 11.78% | 6.20% |
+
+Emissions beat fees over the 7- and 30-day windows, so staking is the right default — but the two
+are the same order of magnitude and the last day flipped. This is a monitoring item, and the first
+candidate for v2 (see below).
+
+### Swap venue — Aerodrome Slipstream CL pool, tick spacing 100
+
+Converting USDC into a 50/50 position needs a swap, and the swap is where a zap actually loses
+money. Executing it against the v2 curve moves the very pool the vault is about to join. Executing
+it against concentrated liquidity does not:
+
+| swap size | v2 volatile pool | Slipstream CL (ts 100) | advantage |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| 10,000 USDC | 4.2904 WETH | 4.3196 WETH | +68 bps |
+| 50,000 USDC | 21.2489 WETH | 21.5900 WETH | +160 bps |
+| 250,000 USDC | 101.4428 WETH | 107.7487 WETH | +621 bps |
+
+The CL pool `0xb2cc224c1c9feE385f8ad6a55b4d94E92359DC59` holds ~$10.3M, charges 0.0379% versus the
+v2 pool's 0.30%, and its active liquidity makes large tickets cheap. Adding liquidity afterwards is
+pro rata and moves no price at all, so routing the swap elsewhere removes essentially the whole
+cost. End-to-end, the measured zap cost (`test_ZapCostByDepositSize`) is:
+
+| deposit | zap cost |
+| --- | --- |
+| 10,000 USDC | −2 bps (a small gain: the CL pool was a touch cheaper than the oracle) |
+| 100,000 USDC | 0 bps |
+| 500,000 USDC | 9 bps |
+
+For comparison, an earlier build of this strategy that routed the swap through the v2 pool itself
+lost **63 bps** on the same 100,000 USDC deposit, and a 500,000 one would not have fit inside the
+strategy's own loss guard at all. Full deposit → deploy → exit round trip today: **9 bps**, exit fee
+included.
+
+Swaps use `SwapRouter` `0xBE6D8f0d05cC4be24d5167a3eF062215bE6D18a5` (verified: its `factory()` is the
+Slipstream `CLFactory` `0x5e7BB104d84c7CB9B682AaC2F3d509f5F406809A`, and its `exactInputSingle`
+takes a `tickSpacing`, not a `fee`).
+
+The AERO sale stays on the v2 router, through the AERO/USDC volatile pool
+`0x6cDcb1C4A4D1C3C6d054b27AC5B77e89eAFb971d` (~$14.1M USDC side). A daily harvest sells a few
+hundred dollars of AERO; that pool is deep enough that the routing question does not arise.
+
+### Price source — Chainlink on Base
+
+* ETH/USD `0x71041dddad3595F9CEd3DcCFBe3D1F4b0a16Bb70` (8 dp, observed updating every ~5 min)
+* USDC/USD `0x7e860098F58bBFC8648a4311b374B1D669a2bc6B` (8 dp)
+* AERO/USD `0x4EC5970fC728C5f65ba413992CD5fF6FD70fcfF0` (8 dp; its $0.4758 was within 0.4% of the DEX price at the
+  pinned block)
+
+A vault that prices its LP from the pool it is invested in can be moved by anyone with a flash loan.
+So every number the vault reports comes from these feeds instead, and the LP is valued with the
+**fair-reserves** formula `2 · sqrt(k · p)` — the value the pool would have after being arbitraged
+back to the oracle price `p`. Only fees move `k`, so a swap cannot move the share price: pushing
+1,000,000 USDC through the pool changes `totalAssets()` by less than 0.5%
+(`test_ShareValueSurvivesSpotManipulation`).
+
+Each feed has its own staleness bound (ETH 1h, USDC/AERO 26h, all owner-adjustable) and a
+positive-answer check. If a feed goes stale the vault **fails closed** — deposits, withdrawals and
+harvests all revert until it recovers. Reading USDC/USD as well as ETH/USD means a USDC depeg is
+priced in rather than assumed away (`test_UsdcDepegRepricesThePosition`).
+
+## Safety model
+
+* **Share price**: oracle-priced, fair-reserves LP valuation; unclaimed AERO is excluded from
+  `totalAssets()` so nobody can deposit just before a harvest to capture other people's rewards.
+* **Every swap** has a floor derived from Chainlink, not from the pool being traded.
+* **Every deploy and unwind** is bracketed by a `totalAssets()` check: if the round trip lost more
+  than `maxValueLossBps`, the whole transaction reverts.
+* **Adding liquidity** is refused while the LP pool's spot price is more than `maxPoolDeviationBps`
+  (default 1%) away from the oracle, because adding into a skewed pool donates value to arbitrageurs.
+* **Exit fee** (default 10 bps, capped at 100) stays in the vault. Unwinding costs a swap; without
+  the fee the exiting user would push that cost onto everyone who stays.
+* **Inflation attack**: 6-decimal virtual-share offset. A 100,000 USDC donation against a 1-wei
+  first deposit costs the next depositor rounding dust (`test_FirstDepositorCannotInflateSharePrice`).
+* **Roles**: owner (multisig) for parameters, migration and `emergencyExit`; keeper for `harvest`,
+  `deployIdle` and `pause`. Neither can withdraw user funds to an arbitrary address.
+* **Emergency**: `emergencyExit()` unwinds everything to USDC inside the strategy and pauses it;
+  users keep withdrawing normally. `setStrategy()` drains the old strategy before switching and
+  reverts if more than 1 USDC is left behind. Note that unwinding needs a live oracle, so if the
+  emergency *is* a dead feed, the owner must widen `setFeedMaxAges()` before exiting.
+
+## Known limitations (v1)
+
+* **Impermanent loss is real.** This is a 50/50 USDC/WETH position: a depositor is half long ETH.
+  The vault is a yield product, not a stablecoin product, and `totalAssets()` will move with ETH.
+* **Fees vs emissions is a fixed choice.** The strategy always stakes. Given the table above, the
+  first v2 feature should be a keeper-flippable mode that holds the LP unstaked and calls
+  `pool.claimFees()` when fee APR exceeds emissions APR.
+* **Very large withdrawals can revert** with `InsufficientLiquidity` rather than silently paying
+  less. Exit in pieces, or have the keeper unwind first. The same applies to migrating a very large
+  position in one transaction: the unwind must fit inside `maxValueLossBps`.
+* **Single gauge, single pool.** If Aerodrome voters kill the gauge, emissions stop; the position
+  stays intact and `emergencyExit()` unwinds it, but there is no automatic fallback.
+* **Fork tests mock feed timestamps after time travel** (`_warp`), since warping a fork freezes
+  Chainlink and the strategy correctly treats frozen feeds as stale.
+* Not audited.
